<metadata><name>Peshtani - St Spas - Galičica pass - Peshtani</name><desc>A west-facing trail with fairly even, steady climbing that the park calls distinctly sporty. The lower part runs through low vegetation, the upper part through forest. The ground is hard and stony, grassy in places. https://galicica.finereli.com/routes/peshtani-st-spas-galicica-pass-peshtani/</desc><link href="https://galicica.finereli.com/"><text>galicica.finereli.com</text></link><copyright author="NP Galičica (trail lines), OpenStreetMap contributors (places, G-6)"><license>https://galicica.finereli.com/about/#license</license></copyright></metadata>
<wpt lat="41.015725" lon="20.810024"><name>Start: Peshtani village</name><desc>Peshtani village to Galičica pass (regional road R-504): 8.3 km, 5 h 30 min, moderate</desc><sym>Trail Head</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="40.959764" lon="20.813707"><name>Start: Galičica pass (regional road R-504)</name><desc>Galičica pass (regional road R-504) to Peshtani village: 8.3 km, 2 h 30 min, easy</desc><sym>Trail Head</sym></wpt>
<trk><name>T-7: the MTB-6 junction to the Galičica pass road</name><desc>T-7 is one of Galičica National Park's harder and longer hiking trails, with more climbing. It runs 4.5 km from the MTB-6 junction to the Galičica pass road, climbing about 531 m and descending 0 m in the direction drawn, between 1,029 m and 1,563 m.</desc><type>T</type><extensions><gpxx:TrackExtension><gpxx:DisplayColor>DarkGreen</gpxx:DisplayColor></gpxx:TrackExtension><gpx_style:line><gpx_style:color>1F7A3D</gpx_style:color><gpx_style:width>4</gpx_style:width></gpx_style:line></extensions><trkseg><trkpt lat="40.990891" lon="20.817455"><ele>1031</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.990784" lon="20.817832"><ele>1033</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.990784" lon="20.817832"><ele>1033</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.990784" lon="20.817835"><ele>1033</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.990787" lon="20.817849"><ele>1033</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.990799" lon="20.817882"><ele>1033</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.990453" lon="20.818069"><ele>1031</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.990458" lon="20.818144"><ele>1031</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.990158" lon="20.818257"><ele>1029</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.990083" lon="20.818297"><ele>1030</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.989999" lon="20.818326"><ele>1030</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.989572" lon="20.818722"><ele>1031</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.989118" lon="20.818801"><ele>1036</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.988646" lon="20.818652"><ele>1038</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.988327" lon="20.818829"><ele>1050</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.988001" lon="20.818709"><ele>1050</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.987171" lon="20.818963"><ele>1066</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.986889" lon="20.819225"><ele>1074</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.986396" lon="20.819194"><ele>1080</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.986193" lon="20.819441"><ele>1091</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.985662" lon="20.819224"><ele>1091</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.985237" lon="20.819491"><ele>1107</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="40.984747" lon="20.819364"><ele>1107</ele></tr